  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Major care commitments (20,000 more nurses, 8,000 more GPs, 3,000 more midwives; integrate physical, mental and social care; parity for mental health; end 15‑minute care visits; recruit 5,000 home‑care workers); strong equality measures (restore 50p top rate, create 10p starting rate, abolish non‑dom status, promote the Living Wage and raise the minimum wage, ban exploitative zero‑hours, renters’ rights incl. three‑year tenancies and caps on rent rises, abolish the Bedroom Tax, expand free childcare, require gender pay gap reporting, race equality strategy); proportionality/fairness (tough anti‑avoidance, rebalanced corporate governance to curb excessive pay, apprenticeship guarantee for leavers with the grades). TEXT_D: Care elements (extra £12bn for the NHS; more GPs, nurses, midwives; mental health and carers’ allowance boosts) paired with strong loyalty/authority framing (leave the EU; five‑year moratorium on unskilled immigration; prefer British workers; restrict social housing/Help to Buy to citizens or 5‑year contributors; +6,000 police/prison/Border posts; leave the ECHR; deport foreign offenders; promote British values); tax changes (abolish inheritance tax; raise 40% threshold; new 30% band) and contribution‑based access to benefits/NHS reflect proportionality more than equality; cut aid to 0.2% GNI.",
